 {:lawyer/id "legal500-766975"
  :lawyer/name-en "David Azcue"
  :lawyer/title "David Azcue is a Partner in Simpson Thacher's Tokyo office, and co-heads the Firm's Private Funds Practice in Japan. He joined the Firm in 2006 and has spent 16 years in the Firm’s Tokyo office and 2 years in the Firm’s Beijing office. David’s practice focuses on advising fund sponsors in connection with all aspects of fundraising across a broad range of asset classes, co-investments, GP stakes, and secondary transactions. He also advises sponsors on structuring, financing, operations, and other related matters. He represented many of the leading sponsors and asset managers in Japan and across Asia. David has also been a speaker and moderator at various conferences, including the Fund Finance Associates (FFA) Japan and APAC Symposium in 2024, and frequently writes about private equity trends and developments in Asia."
